# The report's up-arrow (spec 06 §7 Q98): a click on a sector with several objects lists
# them; a report opened from that list has the arrow at its top right, which brings the
# list back; the report the game opens at the start, and one opened by a click on a
# sector with a single object, have none (docs/BUILDING.md "Input scripts").
# layouts: both (also plays at 800x600: run_input_tests.py --small)
options --quick-start=Terran --empires=4 --seed=7 --open=none --layout=1024x768 --size=1280x800

wait-screen game
wait 5
assert-absent item:##toList
# A planet with two moons in its sector (the "3" beside it): the list of the three.
click sector:9,3
wait-for item:report:planet
assert-absent item:##toList
click item:report:planet nth=2
wait-gone item:report:planet
assert-present item:##toList
assert-inside item:##toList tag:panel:report
click item:##toList
wait-for item:report:planet nth=3
click item:report:planet nth=1
assert-present item:##toList
# The home sector holds only the homeworld: its report has no arrow.
click sector:home
wait 2
assert-absent item:##toList
